DARK PAWNS -- LICENSING

Dark Pawns is a non-commercial hobby project. Please read this whole file:
the game you are looking at carries obligations from 1990 that are still
in force, and this file exists so nobody has to learn about them the
hard way.

This repository contains three license texts:

  LICENSE              this file: the summary, the history, and the MIT
                       License for original new code
  LICENSE.CircleMUD    the CircleMUD License, with the DikuMUD License
                       appended, exactly as distributed with the Dark Pawns
                       2.2 C code base (its src/license)
  LICENSE.DikuMUD      the DikuMUD License on its own, extracted byte for
                       byte from the end of LICENSE.CircleMUD, which
                       describes that part as "the original, unmodified
                       DikuMUD license"

=====================================================================
1. DIKUMUD AND CIRCLEMUD LICENSES (APPLY TO THE GAME)
=====================================================================

The Dark Pawns game is derived from CircleMUD 3.0 by Jeremy Elson, which is itself derived from DikuMUD Gamma 0.0 by Hans
Henrik Staerfeldt, Katja Nyboe, Tom Madsen, Michael Seifert, and Sebastian
Hammer. This covers the original C source kept in src/ as a read-only
reference, and the Go port: a translation of derived code is itself a
derivative work, and the CircleMUD license explicitly rejects the "but we
rewrote it" defense.

Those portions are subject to the CircleMUD License and the DikuMUD
License, reproduced verbatim in LICENSE.CircleMUD and LICENSE.DikuMUD.
In short:

  a. STRICTLY NON-COMMERCIAL. You may not charge money, accept donations,
     or receive any compensation in connection with the game -- no fees
     to play, no paid perks, no donations for hardware, no reimbursement
     of hosting costs, no selling the code or a hosting service.
     (CircleMUD License, condition 1; DikuMUD License: "under no
     circumstances make profit on *ANY* part of DikuMud in any possible
     way.")

  b. CREDIT THE AUTHORS. The login greeting names the DikuMUD and
     CircleMUD creators, the in-game 'credits' command shows the
     CircleMUD/DikuMUD credits file unaltered, and the CIRCLEMUD help
     entry is kept intact. Do not remove or alter these.

  c. SHIP THE LICENSES. The CircleMUD and DikuMUD license texts must
     accompany every copy or distribution of the game, in whole or in
     part, "as is". Do not remove copyright, licensing or authorship
     notices from any source file.

  d. TELL THE DIKUMUD AUTHORS. The DikuMUD License also asks anyone who
     sets up a running copy, or publishes any part of DikuMud, to notify
     its authors first. The 1990 addresses it lists are long gone; the
     clause is reproduced here so this summary does not pretend the
     list above is complete.

This summary is a reading aid, not a substitute: the license texts govern.

Historical note: in February 1999, on rec.games.mud.diku, Dark Pawns'
administrator was publicly and thoroughly corrected on exactly these
points after an advertisement described the game as "completely original"
while the login screen said "Based on CircleMUD 3.0". The full thread is
archived here:

    https://darkpawns.org/archive/usenet-1999-02-11-license-dispute

This file exists so that never happens again.

=====================================================================
2. ORIGINAL DARK PAWNS CONTENT
=====================================================================

The original Dark Pawns world, help text and C code additions are
Copyright (c) 1997-2010 the Dark Pawns Coding Team. They were published
by R.E. Paret (Frontline) at https://github.com/rparet/darkpawns "at the
request of some nostalgic former players". That repository carries no
license file. This project uses that content in good faith, with full
credit to its authors, and is seeking their explicit permission.

